# Migration assessment: `OVHcloud`, `Scaleway`

- Inventory file: `inventory.json`
- Source: `aws`
- Catalog: `OVHcloud` snapshot from `https://www.ovhcloud.com/en/public-cloud/prices/`, retrieved 2026-11-08
- Catalog: `Scaleway` snapshot from `https://www.scaleway.com/en/pricing/`, retrieved 2026-11-01

## Comparison

### Summary

| Fit | `OVHcloud` | `Scaleway` |
|---|---|---|
| direct | 2 | 2 |
| partial | 1 | 1 |
| none | 0 | 0 |
| total | 3 | 3 |

### Resources

| ID | Category | `OVHcloud` fit | `OVHcloud` best offering | `Scaleway` fit | `Scaleway` best offering |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `bucket-example` | `storage.object` | direct | `Object Storage` | direct | `Object Storage` |
| `db-example` | `database.postgresql` | direct | `Managed PostgreSQL` | direct | `Managed Database for PostgreSQL` |
| `partial-example` | `compute.vm` | partial | `Public Cloud Instances` | partial | `Instances` |

### Blockers on every target

None.

## `OVHcloud`

### Summary

| Fit | Resources |
|---|---|
| direct | 2 |
| partial | 1 |
| none | 0 |
| total | 3 |

### Resources

| ID | Raw type | Category | Fit | Best offering | Reasons |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `bucket-example` | `AWS::S3::Bucket` | `storage.object` | direct | `Object Storage` | `Object Storage` offers every capability the resource uses |
| `db-example` | `AWS::RDS::DBInstance` | `database.postgresql` | direct | `Managed PostgreSQL` | `Managed PostgreSQL` offers every capability the resource uses |
| `partial-example` | `AWS::EC2::Instance` | `compute.vm` | partial | `Public Cloud Instances` | `Public Cloud Instances` does not offer `node-high-availability` |

### Required changes

- `partial-example`: `node-high-availability` (not offered by `Public Cloud Instances`)

### Blockers

None.

## `Scaleway`

### Summary

| Fit | Resources |
|---|---|
| direct | 2 |
| partial | 1 |
| none | 0 |
| total | 3 |

### Resources

| ID | Raw type | Category | Fit | Best offering | Reasons |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `bucket-example` | `AWS::S3::Bucket` | `storage.object` | direct | `Object Storage` | `Object Storage` offers every capability the resource uses |
| `db-example` | `AWS::RDS::DBInstance` | `database.postgresql` | direct | `Managed Database for PostgreSQL` (tie: `Managed Database for PostgreSQL and MySQL`) | `Managed Database for PostgreSQL` offers every capability the resource uses |
| `partial-example` | `AWS::EC2::Instance` | `compute.vm` | partial | `Instances` | `Instances` does not offer `node-high-availability`; `Instances` does not offer `snapshots` |

### Required changes

- `partial-example`: `node-high-availability`, `snapshots` (not offered by `Instances`)

### Blockers

None.
